{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"ADEVX-134 verified against production. Re-ran 5d28 and got status pr_promoted, ci_status passed, repair_attempts 1, opening and promoting navapbc/archive-massgov-pfml#21 with exactly the one declared file. excluded_paths was empty on every production run, so the exclusion branch never fired on its own. Closed that gap by replaying the leak inside the production workspace with a pre-staged index, which produced excluded ('portal/next-env.d.ts',) with that file byte-identical to HEAD in the published tree."},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789933499226955001,"uuid":"a89bf3a6-5973-49ce-9231-9bf8d69ef729"}